], 'Player Rating Distribution (White + Black Combined)', 'Count', height=350)

html += f'''
<h3>Rating Differential and Win Probability</h3>

<p>The <strong>rating differential</strong> (white_rating &minus; black_rating) is one of the strongest predictors of game outcome. The correlation between the absolute rating gap and the higher-rated player winning is <strong>r = {ra['correlation_diff_higher_wins']}</strong> &mdash; a meaningful positive relationship.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Metric:</strong> When the rating gap is 0&ndash;50 points, the higher-rated player wins just <strong>{ra['gap_analysis'][0]['higher_rated_win_pct']}%</strong> of decisive games &mdash; essentially a coin flip. But when the gap exceeds 500 points, the favorite wins <strong>{ra['gap_analysis'][5]['higher_rated_win_pct']}%</strong> of the time.
</div>

<table>
  <tr><th>Rating Gap</th><th class="num">Games</th><th class="num">Higher-Rated Win%</th></tr>'''

gap_labels = []
gap_pcts = []
for g in ra['gap_analysis']:
    html += f'''
