html += '''
</table>

<p>The <strong>Van't Kruijs Opening</strong> (1. e3) stands out dramatically: black wins <strong>64.2%</strong> of decisive games, a massive reversal of the typical first-move advantage. This opening is generally considered passive and is often played by beginners or as a "surprise" weapon &mdash; the data suggests it is counterproductive. Similarly, the <strong>Sicilian Defense</strong> and <strong>Scandinavian Defense</strong> show black outperforming, consistent with these defenses' reputation for giving black active counterplay.</p>

